TITLE:: SDGTrack
summary:: one global effect of one orbit as a track: inserts before and after it, and a fader on what it adds
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGInsert, Classes/SDGWindow, Classes/GlobalDirtEffect

DESCRIPTION::
Every global effect of an orbit runs on a track of its own, made by the
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: when it loads: SuperDirt's delay, reverb and
leslie, and whatever code::effects/:: holds. The window's effects tab shows the
selected orbit's tracks as strips. A track belongs to one orbit: the reverb of
orbit 0 and the reverb of orbit 1 are two tracks, with two faders.

code::
t = ~sdg.tracksOf(0).first;                  // orbit 0's first global effect
t.name;                                      // -> global_sdgspace
t.level = 0.5;                               // -6 dB of what it adds; the dry signal stays
~sdg.setTrackEffect(t, \dirt_reverb);        // another effect on the same track, if the orbit has none
~sdg.addTrackInsert(t, \pre, \eq);           // an eq on what goes into it
~sdg.addTrackInsert(t, \post, \compressor);  // a compressor on what comes out
~sdg.moveTrack(t, 1);                        // later in the chain, nothing restarted
~sdg.removeTrack(t);                         // the effect and its inserts out of the orbit
::

subsection:: The signal

In the orbit's code::globalEffects:: a track is

code::
// send, pre inserts, the effect, post inserts, return
::

The effect's code::dryBus:: and code::effectBus:: are two busses of the track's,
put in its state, which link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect#-play:: sends after the
orbit's. The send copies the orbit's dry bus to the first, and the return adds
the second, at the fader's level, to the orbit's effect bus. An effect file
needs to know nothing of this. With the fader at 0 dB and no insert the orbit
sounds as it did without a track (measured: a known gain effect comes out at
1.500 times the dry signal at fader 1, 1.25 at fader 0.5, 1.000 at fader 0).

An effect that also writes to its dry bus, as stock code::dirt_leslie:: does, is
inline: link::#*writesDry:: finds it in its SynthDesc, and its return copies the
track's in bus back over the orbit's dry bus. Its fader still only scales what
it adds, and its pre inserts then also process the dry signal.

Each track uses 2 synths and 2 busses of code::numChannels:: on top of its
effect. They sleep with the orbit, and every event wakes them.

subsection:: Who owns what

The link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: makes and frees tracks. They come back with
the orbit after a cmd-period, with their level and inserts. Reading a file again
keeps its tracks; so does link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-reload::, unless the effect
is gone from the folder. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-free:: removes them and puts
the remaining effects back on the orbit's own busses.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Made by the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::, not by hand.
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.
ARGUMENT:: orbitIndex
the orbit's number.
ARGUMENT:: fx
its link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::.

METHOD:: sendName
The send's effect name; its SynthDef adds the channel count.

METHOD:: returnName
The return's effect name; its SynthDef adds the channel count.

METHOD:: isTrackName
Whether a name is that of a send or a return.
ARGUMENT:: name
a Symbol or String.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: makeDefs
Add the send's and the return's SynthDefs.
ARGUMENT:: numChannels
the channel count.

METHOD:: writesDry
Whether an effect writes to its dry bus as well, by its SynthDef's outputs.
ARGUMENT:: name
the effect's name, without the channel count.
ARGUMENT:: numChannels
the channel count.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: sdg
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

METHOD:: orbitIndex
RETURNS:: the orbit's number.

METHOD:: orbit
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/DirtOrbit::.

METHOD:: fx
RETURNS:: its link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::; nil only during a reload.

METHOD:: name
RETURNS:: the effect's name, a link::Classes/Symbol::.

METHOD:: shortName
What the strip calls it: code::dirt_delay:: is delay, code::global_x:: is x.

METHOD:: id
The number its meter replies carry.

METHOD:: level
The fader, an amplitude from 0 to 4, on what the effect adds to the orbit. It
sends a code::\trackLevel:: notification from the SuperDirtGUI.
ARGUMENT:: amp
the amplitude.

METHOD:: metering
Whether the return sends its levels as code::'/sdgtrack'::, 20 a second. The
window turns this on for the tracks it shows.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: pre
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGInsert::s before the effect, in signal order.

METHOD:: post
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGInsert::s after the effect, in signal order.

METHOD:: inserts
RETURNS:: both lists as one.

METHOD:: insertsAt
ARGUMENT:: place
code::\pre:: or code::\post::.
RETURNS:: the inserts of that place.

METHOD:: busAt
ARGUMENT:: place
code::\pre:: or code::\post::.
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: the inserts of that place process.

METHOD:: inBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: the effect reads as its dry bus.

METHOD:: outBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: the effect writes as its effect bus.

METHOD:: sendFx
RETURNS:: the send, a link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::.

METHOD:: returnFx
RETURNS:: the return, a link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::.

METHOD:: chain
RETURNS:: this track's part of the orbit's code::globalEffects::, in signal order. A VST insert is not in it.

METHOD:: nodes
RETURNS:: the chain's synths in signal order, VST inserts' included.
